# Workload registry

Policy source: `AGENTS.md`. Catalog: `packages/workload-registry/src/workload-registry.ts`.

Every **Cloud Tasks queue**, **Cloud Scheduler job**, **Pub/Sub subscription**, **worker `/tasks/*` route**, and **in-process scheduler** MUST be:

1. Registered in `packages/workload-registry/src/workload-registry.ts`
2. Instrumented with `createWorkloadRunRecorder` / `withWorkloadRun` (`@repo/workload-runs`) at the async entry point

## Lineage

When enqueueing Cloud Tasks, propagate:

- `X-Workload-Run-Parent-Id`
- `X-Workload-Run-Root-Id`

## Coverage

Run before merging changes that add background work:

```bash
pnpm check:workload-coverage
```

(or `pnpm exec tsx scripts/check-workload-coverage.ts`)

## Opt-out

Only with an explicit comment next to the trigger:

```ts
// workload-registry:ignore reason=...
```

## Docs

- `docs/infrastructure/workload-inventory.md`
- `docs/infrastructure/workload-inventory-by-entity.md`
- `docs/infrastructure/workload-system-catalog.md`

## Do not

- Add Terraform queues/schedulers without registry entries
- Add worker routes that skip run recording
- Use ignore comments to avoid inventory without a real reason

## Enforcement

- `pnpm check:workload-coverage`
- Code review against `AGENTS.md`

